Compare backup times in the right order

GuiMap::TryBackup() copies a map into the backups folder at most once every
minSecondsBetweenBackups (1800 seconds). The interval test reads

    difftime(lastBackupTime, currTime) >= minSecondsBetweenBackups

but difftime(a, b) returns a - b, and lastBackupTime is never later than
currTime, so once a map has been backed up the test cannot pass again: no
further backup of that map is made for as long as it stays open. Swap the
arguments.

Upstream: not submitted yet
Applies-to: all environments

diff --git a/src/chkdraft/ui/main_windows/gui_map.cpp b/src/chkdraft/ui/main_windows/gui_map.cpp
index 840f105..6ea2bb5 100644
--- a/src/chkdraft/ui/main_windows/gui_map.cpp
+++ b/src/chkdraft/ui/main_windows/gui_map.cpp
@@ -4070,7 +4070,7 @@ bool GuiMap::TryBackup(bool & outCopyFailed)
     {
         time_t currTime = time(0);
         // If there are no previous backups or enough time has elapsed since the last...
-        if ( (lastBackupTime == -1 || difftime(lastBackupTime, currTime) >= minSecondsBetweenBackups) )
+        if ( (lastBackupTime == -1 || difftime(currTime, lastBackupTime) >= minSecondsBetweenBackups) )
